14.6 Closed stage-operation registry

The exact stage-operation set is:

- Stage 01: COMPLETE, SEMANTIC_CHALLENGE, RECONCILE_INTAKE;
- Stage 02: COMPLETE, SEARCH_ADEQUACY_REVIEW, RECONCILE_SOURCE_SEARCH;
- Stage 03: COMPLETE, SEMANTIC_CHALLENGE, RECONCILE_RESEARCH;
- Stage 04: COMPLETE, DISPOSITION_CHALLENGE, ATOMICITY_CHALLENGE, RECONCILE_REQUIREMENTS;
- Stage 05: COMPLETE, SEMANTIC_REVIEW, RECONCILE_REQUIREMENT_SET;
- Stage 06: COMPLETE, PROOF_REVIEW, RECONCILE_VERIFICATION_SUITE;
- Stage 07: COMPLETE, EXECUTE_FAILURE_TEST;
- Stage 08: COMPLETE;
- Stage 09: COMPLETE;
- Stage 10: FREEZE;
- Stage 11: EXECUTE_RUN;
- Stage 12: VERIFY;
- Stage 13: COMPARE;
- Stage 14: ROOT_CAUSE;
- Stage 15: COMPLETE, EXECUTE_REGRESSION;
- Stage 16: CORRECT;
- Stage 17: FREEZE, EXECUTE_RUN, VERIFY, COMPARE, ROOT_CAUSE, REGRESSION, CORRECT;
- Stage 18: COMPLETE;
- Stage 19: CONFIRM_FREEZE, EXECUTE_RUN, VERIFY, COMPARE, REGRESSION_VERIFY, CONFIRM;
- Stage 20: FREEZE_BASELINE;
- Stage 21: COMPLETE;
- Stage 22: RUN_NATIVE_TESTS, EXECUTE_EXTERNAL_TEST;
- Stage 23: COMPLETE;
- Stage 24: RUN_NATIVE_ATTACKS, COMPLETE;
- Stage 25: FREEZE_DELIVERY_CANDIDATE, COMPLETE;
- Stage 26: COMPLETE, SEMANTIC_REVIEW, RECONCILE;
- Stage 27: CALCULATE_RELEASE, ADVISORY_REVIEW;
- Stage 28: VERIFY_IDENTITY, CAPTURE_DELIVERY_INTENT;
- Stage 29: CALCULATE_EVIDENCE_CHAINS, INVESTIGATE_MISSING_EVIDENCE;
- Stage 30: CALCULATE_TERMINAL, EXPORT_OR_SHARE_AUTHORIZED_ARTIFACTS, RECORD_DELIVERY_EVIDENCE.

16.1 Verification phase and due-stage model

Every release-bearing proposition, proof obligation, test, observation obligation, regression, and deferred failure test declares:

- VERIFICATION_PHASE: PREPRODUCT_ITERATION, FINAL_PRODUCT_DETERMINISTIC, FINAL_PRODUCT_MEANING, FINAL_PRODUCT_ADVERSARIAL, FINAL_REPRESENTATION, DELIVERY_IDENTITY, EVIDENCE_CLOSURE, REGISTRY_CLOSURE, or TERMINAL_DELIVERY;
- EARLIEST_EXECUTABLE_STAGE;
- REQUIRED_BY_STAGE;
- PER_RUN_REQUIRED;
- FINAL_PRODUCT_REQUIRED;
- DELIVERY_REQUIRED;
- TARGET_AVAILABILITY_CONDITION.

The application derives DUE_NOW only when the current stage is at least EARLIEST_EXECUTABLE_STAGE, the target-availability condition is TRUE, the obligation is current and applicable, and the current stage is at or beyond its REQUIRED_BY_STAGE. UNKNOWN target availability blocks only when the obligation could be due.

Stages 12, 13, 18, and 19 evaluate only current applicable PREPRODUCT_ITERATION obligations whose PER_RUN_REQUIRED value is TRUE and that are due by the relevant stage. Final-product, representation, delivery, evidence-closure, registry-closure, and terminal-delivery obligations do not block Stage 18 or Stage 19 before their targets exist, and Stages 12, 13, 18, and 19 MUST NOT require product-only, representation-only, delivery-only, or terminal-only propositions before their targets exist. They remain preserved as future required obligations and become due at their declared stages.

A deferred target-dependent test becomes due no earlier than the first stage where its target exists and no later than REQUIRED_BY_STAGE. It is never required before the target exists and is never represented as executed before actual execution.

32.2 Stage 07 completion

For every applicable mutation:
- the fixture is identifiable;
- required bytes exist when byte-backed;
- execution occurred through a capable route;
- expected rejection exists;
- actual result exists;
- actual rejection matches expected rejection;
- evidence is sufficient;
- an accepted invalid fixture has a linked validator defect.

Fixture creation is not fixture execution.

32.3 Stage 15 regression

Every confirmed defect requires:
- preserved failure fixture;
- exact reproduction procedure;
- detection method;
- actual pre-correction execution;
- pre-correction failure result;
- sufficient pre-correction evidence;
- correction;
- distinct later corrected execution;
- post-correction success;
- sufficient post-correction evidence;
- permanent active status unless legitimately retired.

A statement that a test "would have detected" the defect is insufficient.
One execution cannot establish both pre-correction failure and later post-correction success.

32.4 Due-stage and isolation rule

A failure or regression test is executed only when its target exists and its current EARLIEST_EXECUTABLE_STAGE has been reached. Its REQUIRED_BY_STAGE may not precede target availability. A not-yet-due test remains registered and visible as future work but does not falsely block a prior convergence stage.

Every negative, mutation, adversarial, storage-failure, parser-hostility, and deliberately invalid fixture executes against isolated disposable state: a test-only project clone, test-only IndexedDB namespace, immutable read-only artifact copy, isolated worker input, or explicitly authorized external sandbox. The suite must prove that no fixture mutated a canonical user project or an unauthorized third-party target. Canonical user projects and third-party systems are never mutation targets unless the exact action is separately authorized and safely bounded.

32.5 Regression retirement

A regression is ACTIVE, SUPERSEDED, or RETIRED. Retirement requires sufficient current evidence that the linked proposition left scope, was replaced so the old mechanism is inapplicable, or the failure mechanism is impossible under the current evidenced architecture; current NOT_APPLICABLE status; required human authorization; independent review; an append-only retirement record; and no current baseline or product dependency. A failing, inconvenient, expensive, unavailable, or flaky regression cannot be retired for that reason. UNKNOWN legitimacy blocks. History is never deleted.

